DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T200000
UID:6a84a8bebe14820029882fff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to use the Brother Persona PRS100 at the Fabrication
  Studio! This class will walk you through the basics of mounting fabric on
 to the embroidery frames and threading the machine.\nThis course is mandat
 ory in order to book the embroidery machine and will be held in the Fabric
 ation Studio on the 2nd floor.\nChildren under 13 must be accompanied by a
 n adult.\nRegistration is required for this class and begins September 1\,
  2026 at 12:30 pm.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes
  of the start of the program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe persona
 l information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library unde
 r the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The infor
 mation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and
  evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can 
 be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 7
 89 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - Fabrication Studio
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84a8bebe14820029882fff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
