BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wychwood Clarinet Choir Performance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T150000
UID:6a3d710bc7d3cd580062ced4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us this fall for a beautiful performance from the Wychwoo
 d Clarinet Choir\, Toronto's premier clarinet ensemble!\nFrom their\nwebsi
 te\n: "Founded in 2009\, the Wychwood Clarinet Choir is directed by condu
 ctor and clarinetist Michele Jacot. The members of the choir include skil
 led clarinetists of all ages who share a love of music making\, friendship
  and fun. The choir’s instrumentation extends from the contrabass clari
 net to the E flat sopranino\, and they regularly perform new compositions 
 and arrangements for the ensemble\, many written by their own Composers’
  Collective. They embrace the ideal of “music for life” and are commit
 ted to sharing our musical experience in educational settings and in the w
 ider community."
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d710bc7d3cd580062ced4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
