BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Michael Kaplan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260901T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T235959
UID:6a73a588e9de65360020af61@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of September\, works by artist Michael Sy
 dney Kaplan will be on display at the Forest Hill branch.\nMichael was bor
 n and raised in Toronto\, Ontario. At birth\, he was given the nickname Mi
 ckey\, and that has been with him ever since. His extended family includes
  a number of professional artists\, actors\, authors\, and politicians. Th
 e arts are in his genes. At the age of 7 or 8\, he was enrolled in paintin
 g classes at The Art Gallery of Ontario upon the insistence of his aunt\, 
 Chip Feldman\, a professional artist herself. Since then\, his artistic te
 achers and mentors have included Jay Dampf and Sam Kara at Dreams Studio\,
  and currently\, Gelen Golrokh at Art Wish.\nOn his first trip to Paris in
  1962\, Mickey fell under the spell of the Impressionists. He loves the li
 ght\, bright images and revealing brush strokes of Monet\, Manet\, and Pis
 sarro\, as demonstrated in his work. His many travels and Jewish heritage 
 have also been significant influences on his work. He often uses as many a
 s a dozen brushes on the same painting to achieve his desired effect. A te
 acher once told him to paint “as if somebody else was paying for [his] s
 upplies."\nMickey's work has been distributed to friends and family as wel
 l as a number of his accounting clients. Much of his work is part of the p
 ermanent collection at the Baycrest Centre. He has participated in a numbe
 r of group exhibits\, and he has donated paintings to numerous fundraising
  initiatives. This is his first solo show.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\
 nArt Exhibit Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for loc
 al artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhib
 its aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neig
 hbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during the Forest Hill branch's ope
 n hours. Please check the\nForest Hill\nbranch page before you visit.\nFre
 e. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Michael Kaplan\; "Shtettle"\; oil.
LOCATION:Forest Hill
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a73a588e9de65360020af61
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
