BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Origami Lotus Flowers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T180000
UID:6a85d95360ccaf01c01f5ccf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This is a six-part workshop series that creates a space for ex
 ploring belonging and not belonging through conversation and hands-on art-
 making. Guided by reflective questions\, participants engage in practices 
 such as origami with washi\, drawing\, dyeing\, and writing\, using the lo
 tus as a shared symbol of transformation and resilience across cultures. T
 he workshops foster an inclusive\, supportive environment\, particularly f
 or those who feel marginalized or disconnected. The series culminates in a
  collaborative public floral installation in the library\, sharing partici
 pants’ work with the wider community.\nLed by artists "Being~inbetween"\
 nThe workshops are open to youth\, ages 13-17\, and require no prior artis
 tic experience.\nWorkshop Dates:\nFriday\, September 11th\nFriday\, Septem
 ber 18th\nFriday\, October 16th\nFriday\, November 6th\nFriday\, November 
 27th\nFriday\, December 18th
LOCATION:Thorncliffe\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85d95360ccaf01c01f5ccf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Machine Embroidery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T120000
UID:6a84a83ebe14820029882fb9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to use the Brother Persona PRS100 at the Fabrication
  Studio! This class will walk you through the basics of mounting fabric on
 to the embroidery frames and threading the machine.\nThis course is mandat
 ory in order to book the embroidery machine and will be held in the Fabric
 ation Studio on the 2nd floor.\nChildren under 13 must be accompanied by a
 n adult.\nRegistration is required for this class and begins September 5\,
