BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist Talk with Paul Ramírez Jonas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T193000
UID:6a8483fe57c264087ad1f3ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:To mark the Canadian premiere of\nPublic Trust\n\, an interact
 ive artwork on display at Fort York branch in celebration of International
  Day of Democracy on September 15\, join acclaimed artist Paul Ramírez J
 onas in conversation with The Bentway’s Director of Programming Anna Gal
 lagher-Ross about his imaginative body of work and his long-time engagemen
 t with democracy\, participation and the public realm.\nFrom projects such
  as\nKey to the City\nand\nThe Commons\nto\nPublic Trust\n\, Ramírez Jona
 s’s works invite people to consider what it means to participate in—an
 d take responsibility for—the cities and communities we share. The conve
 rsation will explore how his practice transforms everyday acts of exchange
 \, promise\, and collective participation into opportunities to imagine ne
 w social contracts.\nToronto Public Library welcomes visitors to participa
 te in\nPublic Trust\nat the Fort York branch from 10:30am-5:30pm on Tuesda
 y\, September 15. Please visit the\nPublic Trust\nevent page\nfor more in
 formation.\nCheck out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate Dem
 ocracy\npage to learn more about Toronto’s upcoming municipal election\,
  access important voter resources\, and discover activities and interactiv
 e library programs for all ages happening at a branch near you.\nPublic Tr
 ust\nis presented by The Bentway in partnership with the Waterfront BIA an
 d in collaboration with Toronto Public Library and Harbourfront Centre.\nT
 his event is generously supported by the McConnell Foundation.\nAbout The 
 Bentway\n:\nAnchored under Toronto’s Gardiner Expressway and guiding its
  complex future\, The Bentway transforms an overlooked stretch of infrastr
 ucture into dynamic public spaces and an innovative platform for year-roun
 d public art experiences\, recreational activities\, and educational progr
 amming. The Bentway is a non-profit organization dedicated to igniting urb
 an imagination\, using the city as site\, subject\, and canvas.\nPublic Tr
 ust\nis presented in partnership with the Waterfront BIA\, and in collabor
 ation with the Toronto Public Library and Harbourfront Center.\nAdditional
  project support provided by the Government of Ontario and Toronto Foundat
 ion.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
  ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Outdoor Terrace
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8483fe57c264087ad1f3ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
