BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI for School: Responsible Success for Teens
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261013T180000
UID:6a9b4e1c1c197d11325d6f1b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI can help with schoolwork. So why does it feel like walking 
 a tightrope? How do you use it for learning without fooling yourself?\nIn 
 this youth-focused class\, you'll learn to use AI as a tutor\, quiz partne
 r\, and explainer\, not an answer machine. You'll practice the tutor loop 
 using provided examples: starting with what your interests are\, what you 
 want to learn\, how you like to learn\, and what you already understand. W
 e'll also cover academic policies around AI and when AI is the wrong tool 
 entirely.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Compu
 ters are provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is requir
 ed and will start September 9\, 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not
  be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nPrivacy and R
 isk Message\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program include
 s activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\
 nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipant
 s are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\,
  which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the
  privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude 
 Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti-Gravit
 y\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLea
 rn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4e1c1c197d11325d6f1b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
