BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:#HackingSocialMedia - 7 Rules for having a great and safe social m
 edia experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T173000
UID:6a7738fbf4e5db3d00c74b02@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An interactive\, multimedia event hosted by Keith McDonald\, F
 ounder of Toronto's the literacyAI project.\nWhether you're just getting s
 tarted or consider yourself a pro\, discover how to work around algorithms
 \nthat strip away the "social" from social media\, protect your privacy\, 
 dodge bogus information\, and break\nfree from the trap of chasing likes\,
  shares\, and follower counts.\nThrough music\, props\, and video clips\, 
 Keith reveals the tricks to master your feeds and experiences on\nTikTok\,
  Instagram\, YouTube\, Roblox\, and others - so you run your apps instead 
 of letting them run you.\nRuns 90 minutes (Includes presentation and audie
 nce Q&A\nPlease register so we know how many people to expect and so you c
 an receive a reminder email the day before the program.\nInformation Colle
 ction Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the T
 oronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20
 (c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program r
 egistration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library han
 dles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@t
 pl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7738fbf4e5db3d00c74b02
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
