BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Music Basics with LMMS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T200000
UID:6a84d430be148200298841f5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for this introductory class on Linux MultiMedia Studi
 o (LMMS)\, a digital audio workstation which includes a sound generation 
 system\, synthesizer\, beat/bassline editor and MIDI control system that c
 an power a small home music studio. Sounds\, tones and rhythms can be gene
 rated\, played\, and artfully arranged to create entire tracks. Tracks can
  then be layered to create songs\, which can later be saved to an output f
 ormat.\nKeyboarding and mouse skills are required.\nRegistration is requir
 ed.\nRegistration begins on September 14th at 12:30pm.\nNote: Your spot wi
 ll not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nInforma
 tion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collecte
 d by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 
 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and
  program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the l
 ibrary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nan
 swerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84d430be148200298841f5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
