BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Trick Or Treaty?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T200000
UID:6a8857c2be1482002988fb99@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In honour of the National Day for Truth & Reconciliation\, att
 end this film screening of the documentary\nTrick Or Treaty?\n\, which is
  "...Enlightening as it is entertaining..." and "...succinctly and powerfu
 lly portrays one community’s attempts to enforce their treaty rights and
  protect their lands\, while also revealing the complexities of treaty agr
 eements..."  Further info about the film at the National Film Board's web
 site:\nhttps://www.nfb.ca/film/trick_...\nTrick Or Treaty?\nis d\nirected
  by acclaimed filmmaker Alanis Obomsawin\, who has created more than 50 fi
 lms.\nThis is a film screening aimed at teens & adults.\nAll are welcome!\
 nDrop-in!\nCourtesy of the National Film Board of Canada.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8857c2be1482002988fb99
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
