BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI and Young People: The Future of Thinking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T160000
UID:6a9b4dee3b6c71003e5de6c7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Today’s youth are the first generation growing up with AI ev
 erywhere. What does that mean for how they think\, make things\, and becom
 e themselves?\nJoin us for an open conversation about AI and youth. This p
 anel discussion will share what young people are actually doing with AI\, 
 what worries them\, and what adults keep getting wrong. Audience questions
  welcome. This is not a lecture about the dangers of cheating or bad choic
 es\; it's the ageless conversation about agency\, creativity\, and thinkin
 g for yourself\, but in the age where digital intelligences are developing
  too.\nFeaturing:\nDashiel Carrera\n\, Incoming Assistant Professor of Art
 s and Machine Creativity\, HKUST\nDiana Maliszewski\n\, Teacher-Librarian\
 , Toronto District School Board\nRonit Novak\n\,\nFounder & Editorial Dire
 ctor of\nThe Grain\nRegistration is required and will start September 9\, 
 2026 at 9:00 AM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes o
 f the start of the program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal 
 information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and e
 valuation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be
  directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b4dee3b6c71003e5de6c7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
