SUMMARY:North York Central Library Film Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T161500
UID:6a7ce5273f18f80030bac161@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an afternoon screening of "Song Sung Blue".
 \nSong Sung Blue\n(2025)\nRunning time: 132 minutes\nDirector: Craig Brewe
 r\nStarring: Hugh Jackman\, Kate Hudson\, and Ella Anderson\nBased on an i
 ncredible true story\, Mike and Claire form a joyous Neil Diamond tribute 
 band called Lightning and Thunder\, rising from a humble garage to dive ba
 r gigs to unexpected hometown stardom. When tragedy strikes\, their love f
 or each other and passion for music give them the strength to overcome har
 dships\, rediscover hope\, and inspire everyone around them.\nThe North Yo
 rk Central Library Film Club meets monthly on Wednesdays. There is a short
 \, informal discussion after the screening\, time permitting.\nRegistratio
 n is not required. Please contact the Browsery Department at 416-395-5672 
 for more information.\nNext dates:\nOctober 21 (Wednesday\, at 2 PM): TBA
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7ce5273f18f80030bac161
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
