BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:#Hacking Social Media: 7 Rules for a Happy & Productive Social Med
 ia Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T140000
UID:6a85ff83f564ef0d72c0f738@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital Inclusion Week: October 4th\, 2026 - October 10th\, 20
 26\nKeith McDonald\, founder of the literacy AI project\, shares his seven
  rules for having fun with social media. Following these rules allows audi
 ences to gain control over algorithms and learn how to recognize and deal 
 with the social pressures\, bullying\, and reputational implications of so
 cial media use. The presentation also includes how to identify and reduce 
 security and privacy risks. This is a multi-media presentation featuring v
 ideo clips\, props\, and group discussions\, and it begins with an opening
  social media song icebreaker.\nSpace is very limited.
LOCATION:Bendale\, Lower Level\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85ff83f564ef0d72c0f738
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
