BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:For Teens: How to Disassemble a Computer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T150000
UID:6a904c99be148200298a6f8a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered what's going on inside a computer? Ever
  wanted to take apart a computer to see? This workshop is your chance! Dur
 ing this workshop\, we'll go over what's inside a computer\, how to proper
 ly open a desktop\, and safety guidelines to follow when it comes to worki
 ng with electronics.\n***\nAbout this event\nDigital Expo 2026 is a dynami
 c day of learning\, exploration and connection focused on shaping a respon
 sible AI future for everyone.\nFeaturing inspiring speakers and interactiv
 e exhibits\, as well as hands-on workshops for adults\, kids and teens\, t
 he event explores how emerging technologies are transforming our lives\, c
 ommunities and civic institutions.\nTogether\, we'll examine the opportuni
 ties and challenges of AI to foster a more informed\, inclusive and empowe
 red digital society that protects Canadians and safeguards democracy.\nChe
 ck out tpl.ca/digitalexpo for more information about the Expo and the work
 shops.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n***
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Novella Room\, 2nd Floor (Appel Salon
 )
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904c99be148200298a6f8a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
