UID:6a7218500d65ac3600444c0e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore how to handle and shoot DSLR and Mirrorless cameras wh
 ile learning the basics of how to take a great photo.\nIf you've ever want
 ed to up your photography game\, whether you just want to get better at ta
 king pictures with your phone\, or you want to graduate to a professional 
 DSLR or mirrorless camera\, join us for a class on the basics of photograp
 hy. We will go over the basic settings that go into a good photo as well a
 s talking about camera settings\, lenses\, and lighting.\nCameras will be
  provided for this program. Number of cameras is limited and participants
  may be asked to share.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Ethennonnhawahstihnen'\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a7218500d65ac3600444c0e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
