DESCRIPTION:Led by TIKA\, the seven session workshop series builds towar
 d the creation of individual vision boards.  Workshops will include: visi
 oning creative futures\, dream mapping\, vision board creation and reflect
 ions.  The series is designed to support Black and BIPOC youth.  TIKA is
  a multidisciplinary artist\, composer\, speaker\, and cultural futurist w
 hose work explores healing\, identity\, and collective transformation. Ref
 lective arts-based experiences creates accessible spaces for imagination a
 nd personal growth.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
